{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F7Sb7BR3RaqRYk6pBZeRsa","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are the full contents of all five files:\n\n## 1. /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs\n\nLines 1-560 define several preset structs used for configuring tank simulation scenarios:\n- `Provenance`: Contains source metadata (title, year, confidence, notes)\n- `SourceWaterPreset`: Water chemistry parameters (temperature, ammonia, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DIC, DOC, DON, alkalinity, minerals, chloride, sulfate)\n- `SubstratePreset`: Substrate layer properties (depth, exchange capacity, detritus trapping, colonizable area, oxygen tendency, grazing surface, nutrient charges)\n- `PlantPreset`: Plant growth parameters (guild, growth rate, uptake biases)\n- `ShrimpPreset`: Shrimp species parameters (optimal temperature range, GH range)\n- `ProcessParamsPreset`: Biochemical process kinetics (mineralization, nitrification, aeration, photosynthesis, respiration, microbial yields, plant/algae growth rates, and many other coefficients)\n- `ScenarioPreset`: Complete scenario configuration (dimensions, fill height, temperature, IDs for water/substrate/plants/shrimp/process params)\n\nThe file includes validation methods and default function implementations for many process parameters.\n\n## 2. /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml\n\nA TOML configuration file for the Neocaridina davidi shrimp species with optimal temperature range 22-26°C, GH 5-10 dGH, and medium-confidence baseline husbandry profile from a 2026 starter preset pack.\n\n## 3. /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs\n\nLibrary module providing scenario loading and state construction utilities:\n- `default_scenario_ids()`: Lists available scenario IDs\n- `load_named_scenario()`: Loads a preset scenario\n- `source_water_to_profile()`: Converts SourceWaterPreset to SourceWaterProfile\n- `process_preset_to_params()`: Converts ProcessParamsPreset to ProcessParams\n- `seeded_state()`: Materializes a scenario preset into a fully resolved TankState with geometry, water chemistry, substrate layers, plant guilds, source-water catalog, and process parameters\n- `cycling_fixture_pair()`: Creates two deterministic cycling tanks (seeded and unseeded) for testing nitrogen cycling\n- `cycling_base_state()`: Shared base state for cycling fixtures (20L nano tank, 25°C, moderate aeration, one fast-stem plant)\n\n## 4. /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs\n\nTest suite for event emission and deduplication:\n- `threshold_events_emit_with_cause_codes()`: Verifies that threshold warning events (ammonia, nitrite, oxygen) emit with non-empty cause codes\n- `threshold_events_are_deduplicated_per_day()`: Confirms events deduplicate within a day but emit again on new days\n- `event_generation_warm_overfed_weak_aeration()`: Integration test with warm 30°C temperature, high pH, weak aeration, strong decomposer biomass, and heavy overfeeding to trigger warnings\n\n## 5. /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml\n\nDefault process parameters TOML file containing all biochemical kinetics coefficients used in the tank simulation (mineralization, nitrification, decomposer, AOB, NOB, comammox kinetics, plant/algae growth rates, heat transfer, feed leaching, etc.) with provenance from 2026 starter preset pack."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab6bd2a96c5196688 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 32881\ntool_uses: 5\nduration_ms: 12910</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24615e58-d50c-4dac-86b6-bdc30a050fb6","uuid":"511e0c0d-6901-4960-8326-2cc585401587","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read the full contents of ALL these files:\n\n1. crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs\n2. crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml\n3. crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs\n4. crates/tank