{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is a software developer implementing a feature specification for Loop 6 of a Rust aquarium/planted tank ecosystem simulator. The feature is \"Shrimp Population Dynamics, Reproduction, Mortality, and Microfauna Turnover.\" The task requires implementing across ~18 files: creating new systems (shrimp.rs, microfauna.rs), expanding types (biology, events, actions, process, state, snapshot), modifying existing systems (nitrogen_cycle, engine), updating data files (TOML presets), updating scenario materialization, and writing comprehensive acceptance/regression tests. The implementation must follow a detailed spec with ~20 acceptance criteria covering hourly stress accumulation, daily condition/reproduction/hatching/mortality, microfauna turnover, state-aware shrimp removal validation, deterministic RNG behavior, and specific event emission with cause codes. The final deliverable should be an implementation notes markdown file.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Rust workspace with crates: tank_core, tank_data, tank_scenarios, tank_tui\n   - Deterministic simulation with ChaCha8Rng (stored RNG, seed-based determinism)\n   - Hourly tick-based simulation with daily aggregation layer\n   - Monod-style kinetics for biological processes\n   - Serde serialization with `#[serde(default)]` for backward compatibility\n   - Temperature-dependent reproduction with piecewise linear factors\n   - Eligible-female proxy formula: `0.5 * adults - berried_females`\n   - GH (General Hardness) derived from Ca/Mg concentrations\n   - NH3 speciation from TAN using pH and temperature\n   - Stability tracking via exponential smoothing of chemistry swings\n   - State-aware action validation (checking queued actions for RemoveShrimp)\n   - Daily pipeline ordering: plants → algae → microfauna → shrimp → biofilter → stability\n   - Mass balance invariants (no negative pools, indices clamped 0..1)\n   - Build environment: `nix-shell -p gcc coreutils cargo rustc`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs**\n     - Core biological type definitions. Extended AnimalState with 5 hourly stress accumulators (`hourly_nh3_stress_accum`, `hourly_nitrite_stress_accum`, `hourly_low_do_stress_accum`, `hourly_heat_stress_accum`, `hourly_instability_stress_accum`), all with `#[serde(default)]`. Added two new structs:\n     ```rust\n     pub struct ShrimpRuntimeParams {\n         pub optimal_temp_min_c: f64,       // 22.0\n         pub optimal_temp_max_c: f64,       // 26.0\n         pub gh_min_d: f64,                 // 5.0\n         pub gh_max_d: f64,                 // 10.0\n         pub base_spawn_rate: f64,          // 0.15\n         pub egg_duration_days: u32,        // 21\n         pub hatch_success_base: f64,       // 0.7\n         pub juvenile_sensitivity: f64,     // 1.5\n         pub high_temp_repro_penalty_start_c: f64, // 28.0\n         pub high_temp_repro_penalty_full_c: f64,   // 33.0\n     }\n     \n     pub struct StabilityTracker {\n         pub prev_temp_c: f64,    // 25.0\n         pub prev_ph: f64,        // 7.0\n         pub prev_gh_d: f64,      // 7.0\n         pub prev_do_mg_l: f64,   // 8.0\n         pub instability_index: f64, // 0.0\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/types/events.rs**\n     - Event type definitions. Added three new EventCause variants: `ChemistryInstability`, `Starvation`, `PoorCondition`.\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs**\n     - Player action and error types. Added new SimError variant:\n     ```rust\n     #[error(\"cannot remove {requested} shrimp, only {available} available\")]\n     ShrimpRemovalExceedsAvailable { requested: u32, available: u32 },\n     ```\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs**\n     - Runtime process parameters. Added 9 new fields with defaults:\n     ```rust\n     // Shrimp dynamics\n     pub shrimp_base_mortality_per_day: f64,                        // 0.002\n     pub shrimp_stress_mortality_scale: f64,                        // 0.15\n     pub shrimp_juvenile_maturation_days: f64,                      // 30.0\n     pub shrimp_periphyton_grazing_g_per_shrimp_per_day: f64,      // 0.01\n     pub shrimp_condition_smoothing: f64,                           // 0.15\n     // Microfauna turnover\n     pub microfauna_mineralization_boost: f64,                      // 0.15\n     pub microfauna_periphyton_consumption: f64,                    // 0.02\n     pub microfauna_population_smoothing: f64,                      // 0.1\n     pub microfauna_shrimp_pressure_threshold: f64,                 // 3.0\n     ```\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs**\n     - Main simulation state. Added two fields to TankState with `#[serde(default)]`:\n     ```rust\n     pub shrimp_params: ShrimpRuntimeParams,\n     pub stability_tracker: StabilityTracker,\n     ```\n     Updated imports and `new()` constructor.\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs**\n     - Observable state snapshot. Added 7 new fields:\n     ```rust\n     pub juveniles_count: u32,\n     pub berried_females_count: u32,\n     pub shrimp_condition_index: f64,\n     pub shrimp_molt_stress_index: f64,\n     pub shrimp_reproductive_readiness: f64,\n     pub microfauna_population_index: f64,\n     pub microfauna_grazing_pressure_index: f64,\n     ```\n     Updated `from_state()` to populate them.\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/types/mod.rs**\n     - Module re-exports. Added `ShrimpRuntimeParams, StabilityTracker` to biology exports.\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs** (NEW - ~350 lines)\n     - Complete shrimp lifecycle system. Key public functions:\n       - `step_hourly_shrimp_stress(state)` - accumulates NH3, nitrite, low-DO, heat, instability stress per hour\n       - `step_daily_shrimp(state)` - full daily lifecycle: feeding → condition → molt stress → reproductive readiness → spawning → egg development → juvenile recruitment → mortality → events\n       - `update_stability_tracker(state)` - tracks chemistry swings (temp, pH, GH, DO) with exponential smoothing\n     - Key internal functions: `shrimp_feeding`, `update_condition`, `update_molt_stress`, `update_reproductive_readiness`, `spawning`, `egg_development`, `juvenile_recruitment`, `mortality`, `emit_molt_stress_warning`\n     - Temperature reproduction factor: piecewise linear, 1.0 at 22-26°C, 0.5 at penalty_start (28°C), 0.05 at penalty_full (33°C)\n     - Spawning: `p_spawn = base_spawn_rate * f_temp * f_condition * f_stability * f_mineral`, samples per eligible female from RNG\n     - Egg development: advances daily, resolves at egg_duration_days (21), hatch probability from multiple factors, 25 juveniles per successful clutch\n     - Mortality: probabilistic per-individual RNG rolls, juveniles have higher sensitivity (1.5x)\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/systems/microfauna.rs** (NEW - ~50 lines)\n     - Daily microfauna turnover. Updates `population_index` and `grazing_pressure_index` based on detritus/periphyton resource availability and shrimp grazing pressure. Consumes periphyton and fine detritus modestly. Reference densities: detritus/2.0, periphyton/1.0 (increased from initial 0.5 and 0.3 to fix algae test).\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs**\n     - Added microfauna mineralization boost before decomposer Monod calculation:\n     ```rust\n     let microfauna_boost =\n         1.0 + pp.microfauna_mineralization_boost * state.microfauna.population_index;\n     let decomp_vmax = safe_rate(pp.decomposer_vmax_per_hour) * microfauna_boost;\n     ```\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/systems/mod.rs**\n     - Added `pub mod microfauna;` and `pub mod shrimp;`\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs**\n     - Hourly pipeline: Added `systems::shrimp::step_hourly_shrimp_stress` after DO step, before events\n     - Daily pipeline: Added `systems::microfauna::step_daily_microfauna` and `systems::shrimp::step_daily_shrimp` after algae, before biofilter. Added `systems::shrimp::update_stability_tracker` at end.\n     - State-aware RemoveShrimp validation in `apply_action`:\n     ```rust\n     if let PlayerAction::RemoveShrimp { count } = &action {\n         let mut available = self.state.animal.adults_count as i64;\n         for queued in &self.queued_actions {\n             match queued {\n                 PlayerAction::RemoveShrimp { count: c } => available -= *c as i64,\n                 PlayerAction::AddShrimp { count: c } => available += *c as i64,\n                 _ => {}\n             }\n         }\n         if (*count as i64) > available {\n             return Err(SimError::ShrimpRemovalExceedsAvailable { ... });\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n     - Updated RemoveShrimp in process_action to clamp berried_females_count <= adults_count\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs**\n     - Added: berried_females <= adults clamping, egg_progress_days >= 0, stability_tracker.instability_index clamping\n\n   - **crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs**\n     - Expanded ShrimpPreset with 6 new fields (base_spawn_rate, egg_duration_days, hatch_success_base, juvenile_sensitivity, high_temp_repro_penalty_start_c, high_temp_repro_penalty_full_c) with serde defaults\n     - Added 9 new fields to ProcessParamsPreset for shrimp/microfauna parameters with serde defaults\n     - Added 15 new default functions\n\n   - **crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml**\n     - Added: base_spawn_rate=0.15, egg_duration_days=21, hatch_success_base=0.7, juvenile_sensitivity=1.5, high_temp_repro_penalty_start_c=28.0, high_temp_repro_penalty_full_c=33.0\n\n   - **crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs**\n     - Added ShrimpRuntimeParams import and materialization from shrimp preset in `seeded_state()`\n     - Updated `process_preset_to_params()` with 9 new fields\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/tests/thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs** (NEW)\n     - Mandatory acceptance test: identical stocked scenarios at 25°C and 30°C for 60 days, asserts ≥20% lower reproductive readiness and fewer juveniles at 30°C\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/tests/shrimp_population.rs** (NEW)\n     - 8 tests: spawning_creates_berried_females, hatch_produces_juveniles, egg_failure_under_stress, mortality_under_combined_stress, microfauna_suppression_under_heavy_grazing, shrimp_removal_validation, shrimp_removal_accounts_for_queued_actions, population_fields_never_negative\n\n   - **crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs**\n     - Extended with 3 new tests: shrimp_berried_event_has_cause_codes, egg_failure_event_has_cause_codes, molt_stress_warning_has_cause_codes\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **`cargo` not found**: `cargo check` failed with \"command not found\". Fixed by discovering the build must use `nix-shell -p gcc coreutils cargo rustc --run \"cargo check\"`.\n   - **`cc` linker not found**: Using cargo directly with rustup toolchain failed because no C compiler was available. Fixed with the nix-shell approach above.\n   - **`algae_bloom_conditions_emit_events_and_overfeeding_raises_nuisance` test failure**: The new microfauna turnover system was too responsive to detritus from overfeeding - higher detritus → more microfauna → more algae grazing → lower nuisance index, paradoxically. Fixed by increasing reference densities in microfauna.rs from `detritus_density / 0.5` to `detritus_density / 2.0` and `periphyton_density / 0.3` to `periphyton_density / 1.0`, making microfauna less reactive to short-term feeding pulses.\n   - **`hatch_produces_juveniles` test failure**: \"Adults: 0, Juveniles: 0\" - all 10 shrimp died in 60 days under supposedly good conditions. Root cause: starting alkalinity (3.0 * vol = 108 meq) was exhausted by nitrification alkalinity consumption (~2.28 meq/day from 0.1g daily feed × 16mg N × 0.1428 meq/mg). After ~47 days, alkalinity crashed → pH crashed to 5.5 → massive pH swing detected by stability tracker → instability_index spiked to 1.0 → condition factor dropped to 0 → massive stress mortality. Fix applied: increased alkalinity_meq_total from 3.0*vol to 8.0*vol and added bicarbonate_mg_total = 300.0*vol. **Tests have NOT been re-run after this fix.**\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Successfully implemented the complete shrimp population dynamics system from scratch\n   - Designed temperature reproduction factor to satisfy acceptance criteria (best 22-26°C, clearly worse by 30°C, near-zero by 33°C)\n   - Resolved pre-existing test breakage from microfauna changes without compromising ecological realism\n   - Identified alkalinity exhaustion as root cause of shrimp mass death in test (pH crash → instability → condition collapse → mortality cascade)\n   - Ongoing: Need to re-run tests after the alkalinity fix and clean up unused variable warning\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full feature specification and implementation task. This included the complete spec for Loop 6 (shrimp population dynamics), the master prompt with the full system design, review feedback (none), and instructions to output an implementation notes markdown file. The user also provided system guardrails: keep edits scoped, address required changes explicitly, cite evidence.\n   - Message 2: \"Tool loaded.\" (after TodoWrite tool was loaded via ToolSearch)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Re-run all tests after the alkalinity fix in shrimp_population.rs (test `hatch_produces_juveniles`)\n   - Fix unused variable warning in thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs (line 69: `let hours = 60 * 24;`)\n   - Verify all existing tests still pass (determinism, save_load, water_change_mass_balance, etc.)\n   - Write the implementation notes markdown file (`<TS>-impl-notes.md`) as the final deliverable\n   - The todo list shows items 12 (Write tests) as in_progress and 13 (Build and fix) as pending\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was in the process of fixing failing tests. The most recent action was editing `shrimp_population.rs` to fix the `hatch_produces_juveniles` test by increasing alkalinity from `3.0 * vol` to `8.0 * vol` and adding bicarbonate:\n   ```rust\n   state.water.alkalinity_meq_total = 8.0 * vol; // high buffer to avoid pH crash from nitrification\n   state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total = 8.0 * vol;\n   state.water.bicarbonate_mg_total = 300.0 * vol;\n   ```\n   The tests need to be re-run to verify this fix works. The last test run showed:\n   - 47 tests passed across all test files\n   - 1 test failed: `hatch_produces_juveniles` (\"Adults: 0, Juveniles: 0\")\n   - 1 warning: unused variable `hours` in thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Re-run `nix-shell -p gcc coreutils cargo rustc --run \"cargo test 2>&1\"` to verify the alkalinity fix resolves the `hatch_produces_juveniles` test failure, then fix the unused variable warning, and finally produce the `<TS>-impl-notes.md` deliverable file. The user's task explicitly states: \"VERIFYING your changes compile — after making all changes, run the project's build/check command... and fix any compilation errors before submitting your response\" and the deliverable format requires an Implementation Notes markdown file.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-root-tank-simulation/24615e58-d50c-4dac-86b6-bdc30a050fb6.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24615e58-d50c-4dac-86b6-bdc30a050fb6","uuid":"326ddb1e-ae98-48df-8ff5-ad0ca18cd8fa","isSynthe