{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SqgDApEDcy2DLr8yeiMzdg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so feed_n_to_c_ratio = 0.16 (mg N per mg C). And the feed chain is:1. Feed → particulate organics (immediate, 0.1g deposited)\n2. Particulate → fine detritus: rate = 0.12 per hour. So in 24h: 1 - (1-0.12)^24 = 1 - 0.88^24 = 1 - 0.037 = 0.96. Almost all particulate becomes fine detritus.3. Fine detritus → dissolved DOC/DON: rate = 0.08 per hour. \n\nIn 24 hours, most of the fine detritus dissolves too—about 87% converts to dissolved organic matter. So from the initial 0.1g of feed, roughly 0.084g ends up dissolved after a day. Now I need to figure out how much of that is nitrogen versus carbon using the N-to-C ratio.\n\nThe dissolved nitrogen works out to about 11.6 mg, but the decomposer bacteria have to actually mineralize the dissolved organic nitrogen into ammonia—it doesn't happen instantly. I'm calculating the decomposition rate using Monod kinetics with the decomposer's maximum uptake rate, the available dissolved carbon concentration, and temperature and oxygen correction factors to see how fast this conversion actually proceeds.\n\nOver a full day, the decomposer can process about 83 mg of carbon, which is more than the 72.4 mg of dissolved carbon entering daily, so it can handle the load. That 83 mg of carbon converts to roughly 13 mg of nitrogen as ammonia—which almost exactly matches what the nitrifying bacteria are processing each day. This balance explains why ammonia isn't accumulating rapidly in the system.\n\nThe real issue is that there's a lag in the early days while the feed material dissolves and leaches into the water column, and once the dissolved organic pool builds up, the decomposer starts producing more ammonia than the nitrifiers can handle.\n\nTo fix this in the test, I need either significantly more nitrifying bacteria or less feed. I could reduce the feed to 0.03 grams for lighter supplemental feeding, or I could increase the nitrifier biomass—maybe setting AOB to 1.0 grams and NOB to 0.5 grams. Alternatively, I could just adjust the nitrifier parameters directly in the test setup to give them higher processing capacity. keeping up and even processing DOC from prior days.\n\nThe issue is that the decomposer processes DOC into TAN faster than the AOB can nitrify it. To fix this, I need to either:\n1. Slow down the decomposer (lower vmax or lower biomass)\n2. Speed up the AOB (more biomass or higher vmax)\n\nFor the test, the simplest approach: reduce decomposer biomass significantly (since shrimp aren't supposed to have massive decomposer colonies), increase AOB. Or, make the test feed less.\n\nActually, let me try the simplest approach: reduce the feed to 0.03g (micro-feeding, which is realistic for 10 small shrimp in a periphyton-rich tank) and give very strong nitrification.\n\nOr even simpler: don't feed at all for this test! The shrimp graze on periphyton. Looking at what the test actually needs—spawning, egg development over 21 days, and hatching—the feeding is just maintenance, and with 3.0g of periphyton they should have plenty without supplemental food. The food factor calculation shows they're well-fed from periphyton alone, but I'm noticing the periphyton declines over time as the shrimp graze it and microfauna consume it, dropping to around 1.03g by day 10.\n\nThe real problem is that periphyton depletion combined with TAN accumulation creates a double squeeze: food becomes scarce while water quality degrades. The light grows periphyton but the combined grazing pressure from shrimp and microfauna is depleting it faster than it can regenerate. So I need to balance periphyton growth rate against consumption, and ensure nitrification keeps pace with decomposition.\n\nThe cleanest approach is to dial in minimal feeding at 0.02g daily, establish strong nitrifier populations from the start with high maturity, seed the tank with more periphyton initially around 5.0g so there's still a food buffer after 60 days, and track stability throughout the simulation.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the ammonia toxicity factor—a multiplier of 5 might be too harsh at low concentrations. Since Neocaridina can handle some ammonia and the EPA chronic criterion sits around 0.035 mg/L, I'll test a multiplier of 3 instead, which zeros out at 0.33 mg/L rather than 0.2 mg/L. This gives more realistic tolerance at the lower end while still penalizing higher levels appropriately.\n\nBut the real problem is that I'm fighting periphyton depletion and TAN buildup simultaneously. Instead of tweaking parameters endlessly, I should redesign the test entirely—remove supplemental feeding and rely on periphyton alone, with a well-established nitrification community. That's how shrimp actually thrive in mature tanks.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4521,"cache_read_input_tokens":84570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4521},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24615e58-d50c-4dac-86b6-bdc30a050fb6","uuid":"3a4aad74-4afa-4912-b614-849aa9d44611"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SqgDApEDcy2DLr8yeiMzdg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue is that even with 4x nitrifiers, TAN production from 0.1g feed outpaces nitrification (~13 mg N/day input vs ~13 mg N/day processing), causing a slow accumulation. Plus periphyton depletes to near-zero. Let me adjust the test to truly good conditions: minimal feed, more periphyton, stronger nitrification."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4521,"cache_read_input_tokens":84570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4521},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24615e58-d50c-4dac-86b6-bdc30a050fb6","uuid":"d4c3a884-06fe-4ee8-9a5c-2fd935258ec9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SqgDApEDcy2DLr8yeiMzdg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013EkGzCo4KZvR5yUXVuB7za","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/shrimp_population.rs","old_string":"    state.water.bicarbonate_mg_total = 300.0 * vol;\n    state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g = 3.0;\n\n    state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g = 0.2;\n    state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.4;\n    state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.3;\n    state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g = 0.1;\n    state.filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index = 1.0;","new_string":"    state.water.bicarbonate_mg_total = 300.0 * vol;\n    state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g = 5.0;\n\n    state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g = 0.1;\n    state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.8;\n    state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.5;\n    state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g = 0.15;\n    state.filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index = 1.0;"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4521,"cache_read_input_tokens":84570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4521},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24615e58-d50c-4dac-86b6-bdc30a050fb6","uuid":"a7ee710d-eafc-426d-a10f-95bf41a5a2c6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013EkGzCo4KZvR5yUXVuB7za","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/shrimp_population.rs has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24615e58-d50c-4dac-86b6-bdc30a050fb6","uuid":"2e6abcc5-35fc-4436-956a-4a7889c7794c","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/shrimp_population.rs","oldString":"    state.water.bicarbonate_mg_total = 300.0 * vol;\n    state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g = 3.0;\n\n    state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g = 0.2;\n    state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.4;\n    state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.3;\n    state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g = 0.1;\n    state.filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index = 1.0;","newString":"    state.water.bicarbonate_mg_total = 300.0 * vol;\n    state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g = 5.0;\n\n    state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g = 0.1;\n    state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.8;\n    state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.5;\n    state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g = 0.15;\n    state.filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index = 1.0;","originalFile":"use tank_core::{\n    Engine, EventKind, PlayerAction, ProcessParams, SimError, SimSeed, SimulationEngine, TankState,\n};\n\n/// Creates a well-conditioned tank with shrimp for population tests.\nfn shrimp_test_state(seed: SimSeed) -> TankState {\n    let geometry = tank_core::TankGeometry {\n        length_cm: 40.0,\n        width_cm: 30.0,\n        height_cm: 35.0,\n        fill_height_cm: 30.0,\n        glass_thickness_mm: 5.0,\n        open_top: true,\n        lid_exchange_factor: 0.25,\n    };\n    let water = tank_core::WaterState::default_for_geometry(&geometry);\n\n    let mut state = TankState::new(seed);\n    state.geometry = geometry;\n    state.water = water;\n    state.water.temperature_c = 24.0;\n    state.environment.ambient_temp_c = 24.0;\n\n    let vol = state.geometry.water_volume_l();\n    state.water.calcium_mg_total = 40.0 * vol;\n    state.water.magnesium_mg_total = 10.0 * vol;\n    state.water.alkalinity_meq_total = 8.0 * vol; // high buffer to avoid pH crash from nitrification\n    state.water.dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total = 5.0 * vol;\n    state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total = 8.0 * vol;\n    state.water.bicarbonate_mg_total = 300.0 * vol;\n    state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g = 3.0;\n\n    state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g = 0.2;\n    state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.4;\n    state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.3;\n    state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g = 0.1;\n    state.filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index = 1.0;\n\n    state.hardware.aeration.enabled = true;\n    state.hardware.aeration.intensity = 0.3;\n    state.hardware.light.enabled = true;\n    state.hardware.light.intensity_index = 0.6;\n    state.hardware.light.photoperiod_hours = 8.0;\n\n    state.animal.adults_count = 10;\n    state.animal.condition_index = 0.8;\n    state.animal.molt_stress_index = 0.1;\n    state.animal.reproductive_readiness_index = 0.5;\n\n    state.process_params = ProcessParams::default();\n\n    // Initialize stability tracker from actual state to avoid day-1 instability spike\n    let ca_mg_l = state.water.calcium_mg_total / vol;\n    let mg_mg_l = state.water.magnesium_mg_total / vol;\n    let gh_d = ((2.497 * ca_mg_l) + (4.118 * mg_mg_l)) / 17.848;\n    state.stability_tracker.prev_temp_c = state.water.temperature_c;\n    state.stability_tracker.prev_gh_d = gh_d;\n    state.stability_tracker.prev_do_mg_l = state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total / vol;\n    // pH will be computed on first tick; use a reasonable estimate\n    state.stability_tracker.prev_ph = 7.5;\n\n    state\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn spawning_creates_berried_females() -> Result<(), SimError> {\n    let mut engine = Engine::from_parts(shrimp_test_state(SimSeed(7000)), vec![]);\n\n    // Run for 30 days with light feeding\n    for _ in 0..30 {\n        engine.apply_action(PlayerAction::Feed { grams: 0.1 })?;\n        engine.step_hours(24)?;\n    }\n\n    let state = engine.full_state();\n    let events = &state.event_log;\n\n    // Over 30 days at good conditions, we should see ShrimpBerried events\n    let berried_events = events\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|e| e.kind == EventKind::ShrimpBerried)\n        .count();\n    assert!(\n        berried_events > 0,\n        \"Should have at least one ShrimpBerried event in 30 days of good conditions\"\n    );\n\n    // All ShrimpBerried events must have non-empty cause codes\n    for e in events.iter().filter(|e| e.kind == EventKind::ShrimpBerried) {\n        assert!(!e.cause_codes.is_empty(), \"ShrimpBerried must have cause codes\");\n    }\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn hatch_produces_juveniles() -> Result<(), SimError> {\n    let mut engine = Engine::from_parts(shrimp_test_state(SimSeed(7100)), vec![]);\n\n    // Run for 60 days - enough for spawning + egg development (21 days) + hatching\n    for _ in 0..60 {\n        engine.apply_action(PlayerAction::Feed { grams: 0.1 })?;\n        engine.step_hours(24)?;\n    }\n\n    let snap = engine.snapshot();\n    // In good conditions over 60 days, at least some juveniles should appear\n    // (10 adults, 21-day egg cycle, good conditions)\n    assert!(\n        snap.juveniles_count > 0 || snap.adult_shrimp_count > 10,\n        \"After 60 days in good conditions, population should have grown. \\\n         Adults: {}, Juveniles: {}\",\n        snap.adult_shrimp_count,\n        snap.juveniles_count\n    );\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn egg_failure_under_stress() -> Result<(), SimError> {\n    let mut state = shrimp_test_state(SimSeed(7200));\n    // Force berried state\n    state.animal.berried_females_count = 3;\n    state.animal.egg_progress_days = 20.0; // About to hatch\n\n    // Create stressful conditions: low DO, high temp\n    let vol = state.geometry.water_volume_l();\n    state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total = 2.0 * vol; // Low DO\n    state.water.temperature_c = 32.0;\n    state.environment.ambient_temp_c = 32.0;\n    state.water.calcium_mg_total = 5.0 * vol; // Low minerals\n    state.water.magnesium_mg_total = 1.0 * vol;\n\n    let mut engine = Engine::from_parts(state, vec![]);\n    // Run one day to trigger clutch resolution\n    engine.step_hours(24)?;\n\n    let events = &engine.full_state().event_log;\n    let egg_failures = events\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|e| e.kind == EventKind::EggFailure)\n        .collect::<Vec<_>>();\n\n    // Under these stressful conditions, egg failures should occur\n    assert!(\n        !egg_failures.is_empty(),\n        \"Should have EggFailure events under stress\"\n    );\n\n    // EggFailure must have cause codes tied to oxygen, temperature, minerals, or instability\n    for e in &egg_failures {\n        assert!(!e.cause_codes.is_empty(), \"EggFailure must have non-empty cause_codes\");\n    }\n\n    // Failure invariant: berried_females_count resolved (back to 0)\n    let state = engine.full_state();\n    assert_eq!(state.animal.berried_females_count, 0);\n    assert_eq!(state.animal.egg_progress_days, 0.0);\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn mortality_under_combined_stress() -> Result<(), SimError> {\n    let mut state = shrimp_test_state(SimSeed(7300));\n    state.animal.adults_count = 20;\n    state.animal.juveniles_count = 10;\n\n    // Create combined low-DO + high-NH3 stress\n    let vol = state.geometry.water_volume_l();\n    state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total = 1.5 * vol; // Very low DO\n    state.water.ammonia_total_mg_n_total = 2.0 * vol; // Very high ammonia\n    state.water.alkalinity_meq_total = 8.0 * vol; // High pH -> more NH3\n    state.process_params.reaeration_kla_base = 0.05; // Slow recovery\n\n    let mut engine = Engine::from_parts(state, vec![]);\n\n    // Run 14 days under stress\n    for _ in 0..14 {\n        engine.step_hours(24)?;\n    }\n\n    let snap = engine.snapshot();\n    let total_survivors = snap.adult_shrimp_count + snap.juveniles_count;\n    assert!(\n        total_survivors < 30,\n        \"Population should decline under combined stress. Survivors: {}\",\n        total_survivors\n    );\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn microfauna_suppression_under_heavy_grazing() -> Result<(), SimError> {\n    // Tank with many shrimp should suppress microfauna\n    let mut state = shrimp_test_state(SimSeed(7400));\n    state.animal.adults_count = 50; // Heavy stocking\n    state.microfauna.population_index = 0.8; // Start with healthy microfauna\n\n    let initial_pop = state.microfauna.population_index;\n\n    let mut engine = Engine::from_parts(state, vec![]);\n    for _ in 0..30 {\n        engine.apply_action(PlayerAction::Feed { grams: 0.3 })?;\n        engine.step_hours(24)?;\n    }\n\n    let snap = engine.snapshot();\n    assert!(\n        snap.microfauna_population_index < initial_pop,\n        \"Heavy shrimp grazing should suppress microfauna. Start: {}, End: {}\",\n        initial_pop,\n        snap.microfauna_population_index\n    );\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn shrimp_removal_validation() -> Result<(), SimError> {\n    let mut state = shrimp_test_state(SimSeed(7500));\n    state.animal.adults_count = 5;\n    state.animal.berried_females_count = 2;\n\n    let mut engine = Engine::from_parts(state, vec![]);\n\n    // Try to remove more than available\n    let result = engine.apply_action(PlayerAction::RemoveShrimp { count: 10 });\n    assert!(\n        matches!(result, Err(SimError::ShrimpRemovalExceedsAvailable { .. })),\n        \"Should fail when removing more shrimp than available\"\n    );\n\n    // Verify state is unchanged after failed removal\n    assert_eq!(engine.full_state().animal.adults_count, 5);\n    assert_eq!(engine.full_state().animal.berried_females_count, 2);\n\n    // Remove valid amount\n    engine.apply_action(PlayerAction::RemoveShrimp { count: 3 })?;\n    engine.step_hours(1)?;\n\n    let state = engine.full_state();\n    assert_eq!(state.animal.adults_count, 2);\n    // berried_females_count must be <= adults_count\n    assert!(\n        state.animal.berried_females_count <= state.animal.adults_count,\n        \"berried_females ({}) must be <= adults ({})\",\n        state.animal.berried_females_count,\n        state.animal.adults_count\n    );\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn shrimp_removal_accounts_for_queued_actions() -> Result<(), SimError> {\n    let mut state = shrimp_test_state(SimSeed(7600));\n    state.animal.adults_count = 5;\n\n    let mut engine = Engine::from_parts(state, vec![]);\n\n    // Queue removal of 3\n    engine.apply_action(PlayerAction::RemoveShrimp { count: 3 })?;\n\n    // Try to remove 3 more (only 2 should be available)\n    let result = engine.apply_action(PlayerAction::RemoveShrimp { count: 3 });\n    assert!(\n        matches!(result, Err(SimError::ShrimpRemovalExceedsAvailable { .. })),\n        \"Should fail because only 2 adults remain after pending removal\"\n    );\n\n    // But removing 2 should succeed\n    engine.apply_action(PlayerAction::RemoveShrimp { count: 2 })?;\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn population_fields_never_negative() -> Result<(), SimError> {\n    let mut state = shrimp_test_state(SimSeed(7700));\n    state.animal.adults_count = 3;\n    state.animal.juveniles_count = 2;\n\n    // Very hostile environment\n    let vol = state.geometry.water_volume_l();\n    state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total = 0.5 * vol;\n    state.water.ammonia_total_mg_n_total = 5.0 * vol;\n\n    let mut engine = Engine::from_parts(state, vec![]);\n\n    // Run many days under extreme stress\n    for _ in 0..60 {\n        engine.step_hours(24)?;\n    }\n\n    let state = engine.full_state();\n    // All population counts must be non-negative (u32 can't be negative, but check invariants)\n    assert!(state.animal.condition_index >= 0.0);\n    assert!(state.animal.condition_index <= 1.0);\n    assert!(state.animal.molt_stress_index >= 0.0);\n    assert!(state.animal.molt_stress_index <= 1.0);\n    assert!(state.animal.reproductive_readiness_index >= 0.0);\n    assert!(state.animal.reproductive_readiness_index <= 1.0);\n    assert!(state.animal.berried_females_count <= state.animal.adults_count);\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":28,"oldLines":12,"newStart":28,"newLines":12,"lines":["     state.water.dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total = 5.0 * vol;","     state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total = 8.0 * vol;","     state.water.bicarbonate_mg_total = 300.0 * vol;","-    state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g = 3.0;","+    state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g = 5.0;"," ","-    state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g = 0.2;","-    state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.4;","-    state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.3;","-    state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g = 0.1;","+    state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g = 0.1;","+    state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.8;","+    state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g = 0.5;","+    state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g = 0.15;","     state.filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index = 1.0;"," ","     state.hardware.aeration.enabled = true;"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
