{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WeGNFMfXTUwfe4BciFFJ1D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found it! There are two additional sources of periphyton consumption in the algae system:\n\n1. `periphyton_respiration_g = periphyton_biomass_g * algae_respiration_fraction_per_day`\n2. `periphyton_grazing_g = periphyton_biomass_g * 0.06 * microfauna_grazing`\n\nPlus the surface_cap_factor limits growth. Let me check the defaults for respiration and the periphyton capacity.\n\nThe periphyton_capacity is based on `colonizable_area_m2 * periphyton_capacity_g_per_m2`. Let me check those values.\n\n\nThe respiration rate is likely the culprit here—if `algae_respiration_fraction_per_day` is around 0.3 to 0.5, then even a modest 5.0g of periphyton biomass could be losing 1.5-2.5g daily just to respiration alone. I need to verify what the default value is for this parameter.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2530,"cache_read_input_tokens":97267,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2530},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24615e58-d50c-4dac-86b6-bdc30a050fb6","uuid":"19b796f6-5fc6-4acc-950b-bc97b2efe287"}
