{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BR1jz2UZSNLUxWkckMvzvZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Almost there! All shrimp_population tests pass now. But thermal_reproduction_penalty fails:- Cool (25°C): readiness = 0.0433- Warm (30°C): readiness = 0.0888- Reduction = 1 - 0.0888/0.0433 = -105% (warm has HIGHER readiness!)This is backwards. The 30°C tank has higher reproductive readiness than the 25°C tank. The issue is likely that both tanks have very low readiness (0.04 and 0.09) due to the starvation problem. At such low values, the comparison is essentially noise.The thermal test uses `stocked_scenario` which has different parameters than `shrimp_test_state`. \n\nLooking at the stocked_scenario setup, I see it's configured with weaker nitrification (biofilter_maturity_index = 0.5, lower bacterial populations) and limited periphyton at 2.0g. This creates the same starvation conditions in both tanks, driving readiness down to near-zero where the thermal comparison becomes meaningless. I need to strengthen the stocked_scenario parameters to match the well-fed baseline.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2417,"cache_read_input_tokens":131706,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2417},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24615e58-d50c-4dac-86b6-bdc30a050fb6","uuid":"219f5341-ee3c-46c4-8ffa-84504bef00e2"}
