nitialized from actual chemistry state\n\nThe thermal reproduction penalty test measures readiness at day 20 (before hatching at day 21 triggers population dynamics that would confound the comparison), then continues to day 60 for juvenile count comparison.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Coverage\n\n| Criterion | Status | Evidence |\n|-----------|--------|----------|\n| Hourly stress accumulation (NH3, nitrite, DO, heat, instability) | Pass | `step_hourly_shrimp_stress` in shrimp.rs, tested via condition trajectory in population tests |\n| Daily condition update with exponential smoothing | Pass | `update_condition` with `shrimp_condition_smoothing = 0.15` |\n| Reproductive readiness from temp/condition/stability/molt factors | Pass | `update_reproductive_readiness`, thermal_reproduction_penalty test |\n| Spawning with eligible-female proxy and RNG | Pass | `spawning` function, `spawning_creates_berried_females` test |\n| Egg development with 21-day cycle | Pass | `egg_development`, `hatch_produces_juveniles` test |\n| Hatch success modulated by condition/oxygen/temp/stability/minerals | Pass | `egg_development` hatch probability, `egg_failure_under_stress` test |\n| Juvenile recruitment (30-day maturation) | Pass | `juvenile_recruitment` function |\n| Per-individual RNG mortality with juvenile sensitivity | Pass | `mortality` function with `juvenile_sensitivity = 1.5` |\n| Microfauna population turnover from resources and shrimp pressure | Pass | `step_daily_microfauna`, `microfauna_suppression_under_heavy_grazing` test |\n| Microfauna mineralization boost in nitrogen cycle | Pass | `microfauna_boost` in nitrogen_cycle.rs |\n| State-aware RemoveShrimp with queued-action accounting | Pass | `apply_action` validation, `shrimp_removal_validation` and `shrimp_removal_accounts_for_queued_actions` tests |\n| Population fields never negative, indices clamped 0..1 | Pass | `population_fields_never_negative` test, invariants.rs checks |\n| Event emission with cause codes (Shrimp