it failure events with their causes, and finally I'm tracking the maximum progress across remaining egg cohorts for display purposes.\n\nNow I'm handling the mortality calculations, adjusting both adult and juvenile counts downward, then enforcing the constraint that berried females can't exceed the remaining adult population by removing any excess. I see the issue—the RemoveShrimp handler needs to trim egg cohorts too, but engine.rs can't access that function directly. I should add a method on AnimalState that handles both the berried female count and cohort trimming in one place.\n\nWriting the clamping method...\n\nNow I need to use this in both the RemoveShrimp handler and the mortality logic, and then update invariants.rs to work with the egg_cohorts structure. The egg_progress_days can stay as a derived value since it's still meaningful to clamp it to zero, and the berried <= adults invariant is already covered by the new method.\n\nI should verify that EggCohort is properly exported from the types module.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13047,"cache_read_input_tokens":62014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13047},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0854d63d-3c8e-45e0-9e18-d2c751830c9f","uuid":"eb1e744c-f386-4c97-bdd7-88c7cb5b6ef8"}
