{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"# Implementation Response (Iteration 1)\n## Changes Made\n\n1. **Clutch resolution**: Introduced `EggCohort` with per-cohort progress tracking. Only completed cohorts resolve; newly berried females start at progress 0 in a separate cohort. `berried_females_count` and `egg_progress_days` update only for resolved clutches. Legacy save compatibility is handled via a migration path.\n\n2. **`thermal_reproduction_penalty` test**: Extended the test to run for 60 days instead of 20. It now asserts at least 20% lower readiness and strictly fewer juveniles in the 30°C tank. The scenario uses a large, well-maintained tank with controlled spawn rate to isolate the thermal effect.\n\n3. **Preset validation**: Added `ShrimpPreset::validate()` to check finiteness, non-negativity, range consistency, and probability bounds. Expanded `ProcessParamsPreset::validate()` to cover all shrimp and microfauna fields. `load_shrimp()` now validates before returning.\n\n4. **Verification**: All 73 tests pass.\n\n## Could Not Address\n\nNone."}}
